{"kind":"article","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Articles"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article"],["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Features-Articles","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Dictation","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"metadata":{"images":[{"identifier":"Feature-Dictation.jpg","type":"card"}],"title":"Dictation","roleHeading":"Article","modules":[{"name":"KeyboardKit"}],"role":"article","color":{"standardColorIdentifier":"purple"}},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"This developer guide describes how to set up dictation."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit can perform dictation directly from the keyboard extension by opening the main app to start dictation, then returning to the keyboard to perform dictation. See the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Dictation-Article"},{"text":" article for more information about this feature.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"👑 Dictation requires a KeyboardKit Pro license with "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/ProFeature\/dictation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" support, unless you want to implement the feature from scratch. You can sign up for KeyboardKit Pro from the "},{"identifier":"https:\/\/keyboardkit.com","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A KeyboardKit keyboard can start dictation by triggering the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/dictation"},{"text":" action, which will call the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardController\/performDictation()"},{"text":" function on the controller, which in turn uses the ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardServices\/dictationService"},{"text":" to start dictation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/StandardDictationService"},{"text":" will open the app to start dictation, then return to the keyboard if it has a ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article"},{"text":". The dictation then stays alive in the background, and can be started again without opening the app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":2,"text":"How to set up dictation","type":"heading","anchor":"How-to-set-up-dictation"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Setting up dictation involves adding all required permissions and capabilities to the app, enabling ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing"},{"text":" between the app and its keyboard, and wire up a dictation engine in the main app.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 1. Add Required Permissions","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-1-Add-Required-Permissions"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Before you can start dictation, you must add these required keys to your app’s ","type":"text"},{"code":"Info.plist","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", otherwise your app will crash at runtime:","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["<key>NSMicrophoneUsageDescription<\/key>","<string>Describe why you need microphone access.<\/string>","<key>NSSpeechRecognitionUsageDescription<\/key>","<string>Describe why you need speech recognition.<\/string>"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"This is needed if you use the standard "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyboardKitDictationPlugin"},{"type":"text","text":" engine. A custom engine may need different permissions."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 2. Enable Background Audio","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-2-Enable-Background-Audio"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since in-keyboard dictation requires that the app is kept alive in the background, you must also enable the background audio capability:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"developer-dictation-background-modes","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["<key>UIBackgroundModes<\/key>","<array>","    <string>audio<\/string>","<\/array>"]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"If you don’t use background audio for anything else, you should explain why you need it in AppStore Connect. Here’s a template."}]}],"style":"important","name":"Important","type":"aside"},{"syntax":null,"type":"codeListing","code":["Regarding Audio Background Mode","    ","The keyboard extension in this app has a dictation feature that","launches the main app to start dictation, then reads continuous","updates from the app while the app is in the background.","","Since the app must run in the background, it requires the Audio","Background Mode to avoid that dictation is cancelled. This mode","is only used to keep the dictation alive, and the user can stop","dictation from the main app and keyboard at any time. ","","If you need to locate this feature:","","    1. Enable the keyboard and Full Access in Settings.","    2. Activate the keyboard from any text field.","    3. Start dictation with the keyboard dictation button.","    4. Return to the keyboard to start dictating.","    5. Make sure that the app is not in the foreground.","    6. Verify that dictation is still running.","    7. Verify that you can stop dictation with the mic button.","","Just let us know if you need any more information regarding this."]},{"level":3,"text":"Step 3. Set up an App Group","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-3-Set-up-an-App-Group"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To share data between the main app and its keyboard, you must set up an App Group and enable it for both targets. See "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" for more information."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 4. Set up a Deep Link","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-4-Set-up-a-Deep-Link"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"To make it possible for the keyboard to open the app and start dictation, you must set up a deep link URL scheme to open the main app:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"developer-dictation-url-scheme","type":"image"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add a unique URL scheme for your app to “URL Schemes”, without the “:\/\/” suffix, then add the full scheme to your "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardApp","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":". As you can see in the app above, the official KeyboardKit app uses “keyboardkit:\/\/” as scheme.:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["KeyboardApp(..., deepLinks: .init(app: \"keyboardkit:\/\/\"))"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"KeyboardKit uses <SCHEME>dictation as default dictation deep link (e.g. “keyboardkit:\/\/dictation”), but you can customize it if needed."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Step 5. Set up the Keyboard Extension","type":"heading","anchor":"Step-5-Set-up-the-Keyboard-Extension"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Since dictation will be performed in the main app, your keyboard extension doesn’t have to be prepared in any special way. Just enable data syncing and a deep link, and the keyboard extension will be good to go."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardView","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" will automatically show a "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationKeyboardOverlay","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" whenever dictation is active. You can replace it with the "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardReplacementOverlay(isPresented:content:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" view modifier if you want to use a custom view.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Step 6. Set up the Main Application","level":3,"anchor":"Step-6-Set-up-the-Main-Application","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"To make the app perform dictation, we must apply a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardDictation(withEngine:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" view modifier to the main app content. See the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Plugins-Article","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" article on how to use the standard ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"KeyboardKitDictationPlugin"},{"text":".","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"style":"note","name":"Note","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"KeyboardKit doesn’t include a ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":", since that would require ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"all","type":"text"}]},{"text":" apps that use KeyboardKit to add the permissions above, even if they don’t use dictation. By moving the engine to the dictation plugin, an app can choose if it wants to use dictation.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"type":"aside"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can also implement the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationEngine","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" protocol yourself, for instance if you want to integrate with a custom engine or model.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Step 7. Start dictation","level":3,"anchor":"Step-7-Start-dictation","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"You can now start dictation in your keyboard by triggering the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAction\/dictation","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" action, or by calling the controller ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardInputViewController\/performDictation()","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" or service ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/DictationService\/startDictationFromKeyboard()","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" functions, based on where you start it from. You should prefer using the action.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/StandardDictationService","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" will open the main app with ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppOpenReason\/dictation","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" as ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/KeyboardAppContext\/openReason","type":"reference"},{"text":". Since the ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Host-Article","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" support is limited, we recommend showing a view in the app to tell the user to tap the top-leading back arrow to return to the keyboard.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Custom-Keyboards","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Data-Syncing","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Debugging","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-dSYMs","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Experiments","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Memory-Management","doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/Developer-Themes"],"generated":true}],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/keyboardkit\/developer-dictation"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"references":{"doc://src.KeyboardKit/documentation/KeyboardKit/SwiftUICore/View/keyboardReplacementOverlay(isPresented:content:)":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/src.KeyboardKit\/documentation\/KeyboardKit\/SwiftUICore\/View\/keyboardReplacementOverlay(isPresented:content:)","abstract":[{"text":"This modifier can be used to overlay a keyboard view","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"with a replacement vie